nds exponent notation and basic multiplication can complete the calculation independently after hint 3. However, hint 3 does narrow the problem down to a single concrete computation (6³), which is somewhat close to revealing—though it still requires the student to do the arithmetic.\n\nOverall: The hint ladder is functional and does not cross into answer-revelation. It is practical for the grade band but not particularly creative or deep (it is linear and procedural rather than exploratory).\n']
