he sine of angle θ:\nsin(θ) = opposite/hypotenuse = 1/√5\n\nLet me rationalize this:\nsin(θ) = 1/√5 = √5/5 ≈ 0.447\n\nLooking at the options:\n- Option a: 2 (this is impossible since sine values are between -1 and 1)\n- Option b: 1 (this would mean θ = 90°, which isn\'t the case)\n- Option c: 1/2 = 0.5\n- Option d: √3/2 ≈ 0.866\n\nMy calculated value is 1/√5 = √5/5 ≈ 0.447\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Perhaps there\'s confusion about which angle we\'re measuring. But the problem clearly states "the angle the ramp makes with the ground," which is the angle at the base.\n\nActually, my calculation gives sin(θ) = 1/√5 ≈ 0.447, which doesn\'t exactly match any option. However, option c (1/2 = 0.5) is the closest to my answer.\n\nBut let me double-check if there\'s a simpler interpretation. Sometimes in these problems, people mistakenly use tan instead of sin. The tangent would be: tan(θ) = 1/2, which IS option c. But that\'s not what was asked.\n\nThe correct mathematical answer is sin(θ) = 1/√5, which is approximately 0.447. None of the options match this exactly, but option c (1/2) is the closest.\n']
